# M1c-corrective — com.pos.orchestrator → com.loam.orchestrator + dev-mode-manifest path refresh

2026-04-29. Closes the two coherent residual surfaces the M1.rename
programme + M9 cleanup pass left behind:

1. **`com.pos.orchestrator` launchd label rebrand → `com.loam.orchestrator`.**
   Per `loam-rename-decisions.md` Tier-1 item 4 + the version-suffix-
   drop ruling. The orchestrator's user-agent label was the v1-era
   single-segment shape — never namespaced because it was authored
   pre-#6 and lived under the pre-rename brand. M1c's workspace-
   slug-namespacing rebrand never touched it. 26 source-tree refs
   across 8 files (orchestrator + self-upgrade) rebrand. Includes
   the LIVE config default in `self_upgrade/config.py:39` + the
   plist template filename rename + the 5-arg `test_d2_launchd.py`
   update + 11 docs-narrative refs.

   Archaeological-detector test data in
   `framework/tools/orphan-plist-cleanup/**` and
   `framework/tools/loam-migrate-launchd-labels/tests/test_migrate.py`
   stays AS-IS — the `com.pos.orchestrator` literal there is
   LOAD-BEARING for the tools' mission of detecting pre-pos-v2
   archaeological orphans on hosts. The cleanup tool's
   `Classification.ORPHAN_V1` enum explicitly identifies "v1-era
   shape (e.g. `com.pos.orchestrator`)" as a remediation target.

2. **dev-mode-manifest.yaml stale path refs.** M6c HSF#1 named
   lines 136-137 (now 137-138 post-M6c narrative-edit shift); both
   `glob:` entries reference pre-M1g + pre-M6b.0/M6b.1 paths.
   Update to post-rename + post-MOVE shapes:
     - `tools/pos-amend/**` → `plugins/dev-sdlc/tools/loam-amend/**`
     - `tools/orphan-plist-cleanup/**` → `framework/tools/orphan-plist-cleanup/**`

Operational restart: the running `com.pos.orchestrator` user-agent
job (PID 57302 at plan-time) gets bootout + reinstall under the
new label so the live runtime state matches the source tree.

Structural remedy:

  - `framework/orchestrator/ops/launchd/com.pos.orchestrator.plist.tmpl`
    → MOVE to `com.loam.orchestrator.plist.tmpl` (filename rename;
    content unchanged — the template substitutes ${LABEL} at install
    time, brand-agnostic).
  - `framework/orchestrator/scripts/install_launchd.py` —
    LABEL constant + tmpl path + docstring (3 refs).
  - `framework/orchestrator/tests/test_d2_launchd.py` — tmpl path +
    4 LABEL test args + 1 assertion (5 refs).
  - `framework/orchestrator/docs/operations.md` — 3 grep examples.
  - `framework/orchestrator/docs/measurement-launchd.md` — 8 refs.
  - `framework/self-upgrade/src/loam/self_upgrade/config.py` —
    docstring example + LIVE default field value (2 refs).
  - `framework/self-upgrade/src/loam/self_upgrade/orchestrator_control.py` —
    1 docstring example.
  - `framework/self-upgrade/docs/architecture.md` — 1 yaml example.
  - `framework/self-upgrade/docs/cli-reference.md` — 1 python +
    1 yaml example.
  - `framework/self-upgrade/docs/sequences.md` — 1 sequence-diagram
    launchctl invocation.
  - `plugins/dev-sdlc/dev-mode-manifest.yaml` — 2 `glob:` lines
    (137-138).

AC surface (AC.RNM-1c-fix.1..RNM-1c-fix.5 + AC.RNM-1c-fix.S):

  - AC.RNM-1c-fix.1: all non-historical, non-archaeological-detector
    refs to `com.pos.orchestrator` rebranded to `com.loam.orchestrator`.
  - AC.RNM-1c-fix.2: LIVE config default rebranded.
  - AC.RNM-1c-fix.3: dev-mode-manifest.yaml lines 137-138 reference
    post-M1g + post-M6b.1 paths; both directories exist on disk.
  - AC.RNM-1c-fix.4: orchestrator + self-upgrade + loam-mode tests
    pass.
  - AC.RNM-1c-fix.5: operational launchctl reload — old label gone,
    new label running, plist files swapped on disk.
  - AC.RNM-1c-fix.S: seal-diff invariant — only paths under the 3
    sealed components or universal-paths.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Plist template filename rename (D1): `git mv` to preserve
    history. Renaming the LABEL constant alone would leave a stale
    `com.pos.orchestrator.plist.tmpl` filename matching post-rename
    greppability assertions.
  - Operational reload mechanism (D3): bootout-old + reinstall-new
    via the post-rename `install_launchd.py`. Lossless — orchestrator
    in-process state is rebuilt from `~/.loam/bootstrap.py` on each
    start.
  - Test scope (D5): narrow to the 3 touched components. Per
    `feedback_amendment_dispatch_speedups`.

Out of scope (per plan §8):

  - Commit messages / seal narratives mentioning
    `com.pos.orchestrator` (preserve historical record per Idea 10).
  - Pre-rename plan-doc references in `docs/rebuild/plans/`.
  - `pos-v2-rebuild-proposal.md`.
  - Archaeological-detector test data in
    `framework/tools/orphan-plist-cleanup/**` and
    `framework/tools/loam-migrate-launchd-labels/tests/test_migrate.py`
    (load-bearing).
  - Broader dev-mode-manifest.yaml staleness — `roots:` (lines
    41-64) + `always_loaded:` (lines 78-110) reference top-level
    dirs that MOVED under `framework/` post-M6b.0; HSF#1 in plan
    §16 deferred to a separate `dev-mode-manifest-realignment`
    amendment.
  - Other `com.pos-v2.*` host-launchd labels (M1c migration helper
    territory, not this amendment).
  - M6c graceful-fallthrough-with-detection CDC retroactive
    operationalisation across orchestrator (FIDRAFT-tracked).

BASELINE `6f272ce` (current HEAD post-#92 SHA backfill).
Each component's SEAL_COMMIT sidecar lands at the seal SHA via
`loam amend seal`.
